---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="CAR v0.1 — Machine Authority Protocol" description="Canonical Action Representation v0.1 draft specification. The serializable schema for a proposed AI agent tool call, submitted to the Action Authorization Boundary for evaluation.">
  <div class="container spec-page">
    <div class="rfc-header">Machine Authority Protocol                                           Draft
Canonical Action Representation (CAR) v0.1
Status: DRAFT — not for production use
Published: 2026-05-02</div>

      <section id="abstract">
        <h2>Abstract</h2>
        <p>
          The Canonical Action Representation (CAR) is a standardized, serializable schema for describing
          a proposed AI agent tool call before it executes. A CAR payload encodes the tool name, typed
          arguments, actor identity, delegation chain, session context, and timestamp in a vendor-neutral
          format that any policy engine, audit log, or approval interface can consume. The CAR is the
          input to the Action Authorization Boundary: the enforcement point evaluates a CAR and returns
          a Decision Envelope (ALLOW / DENY / DEFER / REVOKE).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="status">
        <h2>Status of This Document</h2>
        <p>
          This document is a Draft specification of the Machine Authority Protocol. It has not been
          reviewed by any standards body. Feedback is invited via
          <a href="https://github.com/machineauthority/protocol/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Issues</a>.
          This document may change before finalization.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="introduction">
        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          When an AI agent decides to invoke a tool — call an API, write a file, execute a query — the
          reasoning that produced that decision is probabilistic. The action itself is deterministic.
          Identity protocols verify who the agent is. Policy engines evaluate whether a rule says allow.
          But neither defines a common format for representing the proposed action itself, nor a standard
          decision state for deferring it to asynchronous human approval.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Canonical Action Representation fills this gap. CAR is the lingua franca of the Action
          Authorization Boundary: it can be produced by any agent framework, evaluated by any policy
          engine, logged by any audit system, and rendered by any approval interface — without
          vendor-specific schemas or proprietary wire formats.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="conventions">
        <h2>2. Conventions</h2>
        <p>
          The key words <strong>MUST</strong>, <strong>MUST NOT</strong>, <strong>REQUIRED</strong>,
          <strong>SHALL</strong>, <strong>SHALL NOT</strong>, <strong>SHOULD</strong>,
          <strong>SHOULD NOT</strong>, <strong>RECOMMENDED</strong>, <strong>NOT RECOMMENDED</strong>,
          <strong>MAY</strong>, and <strong>OPTIONAL</strong> in this document are to be interpreted as
          described in RFC 2119.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="terminology">
        <h2>3. Terminology</h2>
        <dl>
          <dt>Action Authorization Boundary (AAB)</dt>
          <dd>
            The mandatory enforcement layer between an agent's reasoning and real-world execution.
            Evaluates a CAR and produces a Decision Envelope.
          </dd>

          <dt>Canonical Action Representation (CAR)</dt>
          <dd>
            A serialized JSON object describing a proposed tool call. The input to the AAB.
          </dd>

          <dt>Decision Envelope</dt>
          <dd>
            The response from the AAB to a submitted CAR. Contains one of four states: ALLOW, DENY,
            DEFER, or REVOKE.
          </dd>

          <dt>Actor</dt>
          <dd>
            The AI agent or system submitting a CAR for evaluation.
          </dd>

          <dt>Delegating Principal</dt>
          <dd>
            The human or system that authorized the actor to act. MUST be included when the actor acts
            on behalf of a principal.
          </dd>

          <dt>Enforcement Point</dt>
          <dd>
            The component that receives a CAR, submits it to the AAB, and either executes the action
            (ALLOW), blocks it (DENY), or suspends it (DEFER).
          </dd>

          <dt>Approver</dt>
          <dd>
            The human or system that reviews a deferred action and produces a signed ApprovalDecision.
          </dd>

          <dt>Resume Token</dt>
          <dd>
            An opaque string issued with a DEFER decision that allows the enforcement point to poll for
            or receive the ApprovalDecision.
          </dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section id="car-schema">
        <h2>4. CAR Schema</h2>
        <p>
          A CAR is a JSON object. All fields listed as REQUIRED in this section MUST be present. Fields
          marked OPTIONAL MAY be omitted. The schema is identified by the URI
          <code>https://machineauthority.org/schema/car/v0.1</code> and validates against JSON Schema
          Draft 2020-12.
        </p>

        <h3>4.1 Top-Level Fields</h3>

        <dl>
          <dt>car_version <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. MUST be <code>"0.1"</code> for this specification. Enforcement points MUST reject
            CARs with unrecognized version values.
          </dd>

          <dt>action_id <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String (UUID v4). Uniquely identifies this proposed action. MUST be generated by the
            enforcement point immediately before submission. MUST NOT be reused across distinct
            proposed actions, including retries.
          </dd>

          <dt>tool_name <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. The fully-qualified name of the tool being invoked. SHOULD follow the format
            <code>&#123;namespace&#125;/&#123;tool&#125;</code> (e.g., <code>stripe/charge_card</code>,
            <code>github/create_pr</code>). For MCP tools, this MUST match the tool name in the MCP
            server manifest.
          </dd>

          <dt>arguments <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            Object. The typed arguments passed to the tool. MUST contain all arguments the tool will
            receive at execution. MUST NOT be redacted or summarized. Policy engines depend on the
            completeness and accuracy of this field for evaluation.
          </dd>

          <dt>actor <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            Object. Identifies the agent submitting this CAR. See Section 4.2.
          </dd>

          <dt>session_id <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. An opaque identifier for the agent session in which this action occurs. MUST be
            stable across all CARs generated within a single agent run. Used to correlate related
            actions in audit logs.
          </dd>

          <dt>timestamp <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String (ISO 8601, UTC). The time at which the CAR was generated by the enforcement point.
            MUST be within a reasonable skew tolerance of actual wall-clock time.
          </dd>

          <dt>policy_context <span class="field-tag optional">OPTIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            Object. Additional context the policy engine may use for evaluation. Contents are
            policy-engine-specific. Common fields: <code>environment</code> (string),
            <code>risk_tier</code> (string), <code>mcp_server_id</code> (string).
          </dd>

          <dt>task_id <span class="field-tag optional">OPTIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. For A2A-based agent workflows: the A2A task ID that produced this action.
          </dd>

          <dt>mcp_tool_call_id <span class="field-tag optional">OPTIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. For MCP-based agent workflows: the MCP <code>tool_call_id</code> from the
            originating request.
          </dd>
        </dl>

        <h3>4.2 The actor Object</h3>

        <dl>
          <dt>actor.identity <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            Object. The cryptographic identity of the acting agent, expressed as a discriminated
            union. MUST contain a <code>type</code> field selecting the identity scheme and a
            scheme-specific payload. The three schemes defined by this specification are:
            <br /><br />
            <code>&#123; "type": "spiffe", "uri": "spiffe://acme.com/agents/billing" &#125;</code>
            &mdash; SPIFFE SVID URI (RFC X.509-SVID or JWT-SVID).
            <br /><br />
            <code>&#123; "type": "did", "did": "did:web:acme.com:agents:billing" &#125;</code>
            &mdash; W3C Decentralized Identifier.
            <br /><br />
            <code>&#123; "type": "url", "url": "https://acme.com/.well-known/agent-id/billing" &#125;</code>
            &mdash; HTTPS URL resolving to a signed agent identity document.
            <br /><br />
            Implementations MUST reject CARs with unknown <code>type</code> values. Future
            revisions MAY register additional identity types via the Machine Authority Protocol
            registry.
          </dd>

          <dt>actor.delegation_chain <span class="field-tag optional">OPTIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            Array of <code>actor.identity</code> objects. Ordered list of principals that delegated
            authority to this actor. MUST be present when the actor acts on behalf of a human or
            upstream agent. Each entry MUST conform to the <code>actor.identity</code> discriminated
            union. The first entry is the outermost delegating principal; the last entry is the
            immediate delegator. Maximum depth: 8.
          </dd>

          <dt>actor.agent_version <span class="field-tag optional">OPTIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. Semantic version of the agent software. RECOMMENDED for audit purposes.
          </dd>
        </dl>

        <h3>4.3 Full JSON Schema</h3>

        <pre><code>&#123;
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://machineauthority.org/schema/car/v0.1",
  "title": "Canonical Action Representation",
  "description": "A serialized description of a proposed AI agent tool call, submitted to the Action Authorization Boundary for evaluation.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["car_version", "action_id", "tool_name", "arguments", "actor", "session_id", "timestamp"],
  "properties": &#123;
    "car_version": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["0.1"],
      "description": "REQUIRED. Version of the CAR schema. MUST be '0.1' for this specification."
    &#125;,
    "action_id": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "format": "uuid",
      "description": "REQUIRED. A UUID v4 uniquely identifying this proposed action. MUST be generated by the enforcement point. MUST NOT be reused."
    &#125;,
    "tool_name": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "description": "REQUIRED. The fully-qualified name of the tool being invoked. SHOULD follow the format '&#123;namespace&#125;/&#123;tool&#125;' (e.g., 'stripe/charge_card', 'github/create_pr'). For MCP tools, this MUST match the tool name in the MCP server manifest."
    &#125;,
    "arguments": &#123;
      "type": "object",
      "description": "REQUIRED. The typed arguments passed to the tool. MUST contain all arguments the tool will receive at execution. MUST NOT be redacted or summarized.",
      "additionalProperties": true
    &#125;,
    "actor": &#123;
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["identity"],
      "description": "REQUIRED. Identifies the agent submitting this CAR.",
      "properties": &#123;
        "identity": &#123; "$ref": "#/$defs/identity" &#125;,
        "delegation_chain": &#123;
          "type": "array",
          "description": "OPTIONAL. Ordered list of principals that delegated authority to this actor. Max depth 8.",
          "items": &#123; "$ref": "#/$defs/identity" &#125;,
          "maxItems": 8
        &#125;,
        "agent_version": &#123;
          "type": "string",
          "description": "OPTIONAL. Semantic version of the agent software. RECOMMENDED for audit purposes."
        &#125;
      &#125;
    &#125;,
    "session_id": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "description": "REQUIRED. An opaque string identifying the agent session in which this action occurs. MUST be stable across all CARs in a single agent run."
    &#125;,
    "timestamp": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "REQUIRED. ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) at which the CAR was generated by the enforcement point."
    &#125;,
    "policy_context": &#123;
      "type": "object",
      "description": "OPTIONAL. Additional context the policy engine may use for evaluation. Contents are policy-engine-specific. Common fields: 'environment' (string), 'risk_tier' (string), 'mcp_server_id' (string).",
      "additionalProperties": true
    &#125;,
    "task_id": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OPTIONAL. For A2A-based agent workflows: the A2A task ID that produced this action."
    &#125;,
    "mcp_tool_call_id": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OPTIONAL. For MCP-based agent workflows: the MCP tool_call_id from the originating request."
    &#125;
  &#125;,
  "$defs": &#123;
    "identity": &#123;
      "description": "Discriminated union for agent identity. 'type' selects the scheme.",
      "oneOf": [
        &#123;
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["type", "uri"],
          "properties": &#123;
            "type": &#123; "const": "spiffe" &#125;,
            "uri": &#123; "type": "string", "pattern": "^spiffe://" &#125;
          &#125;
        &#125;,
        &#123;
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["type", "did"],
          "properties": &#123;
            "type": &#123; "const": "did" &#125;,
            "did":  &#123; "type": "string", "pattern": "^did:" &#125;
          &#125;
        &#125;,
        &#123;
          "type": "object",
          "required": ["type", "url"],
          "properties": &#123;
            "type": &#123; "const": "url" &#125;,
            "url":  &#123; "type": "string", "format": "uri", "pattern": "^https://" &#125;
          &#125;
        &#125;
      ]
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="decision-envelope">
        <h2>5. Decision Envelope</h2>
        <p>
          When an enforcement point submits a CAR to the AAB, the AAB MUST respond with a Decision
          Envelope. The Decision Envelope is a JSON object identified by the URI
          <code>https://machineauthority.org/schema/decision-envelope/v0.1</code>.
        </p>

        <h3>5.1 Decision States</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>ALLOW</dt>
          <dd>
            The action is authorized. The enforcement point MAY proceed to execution. MUST check
            <code>expires_at</code> before executing; an expired ALLOW MUST be treated as DENY.
          </dd>

          <dt>DENY</dt>
          <dd>
            The action is not authorized. The enforcement point MUST NOT execute. MUST surface the
            <code>reason_code</code> and <code>reason_detail</code> to the agent so it can adapt or
            halt.
          </dd>

          <dt>DEFER</dt>
          <dd>
            The action requires human (or upstream) approval before it may proceed. The enforcement
            point MUST suspend execution, preserve session state, and poll or subscribe to the
            <code>approver_endpoint</code> using the <code>resume_token</code> until an
            ApprovalDecision is received or <code>defer_payload.expires_at</code> is reached. If
            approval is not received by that time, the enforcement point MUST treat the action as DENY.
          </dd>

          <dt>REVOKE</dt>
          <dd>
            A previously ALLOWed action has been revoked. The enforcement point MUST abort execution
            immediately if in progress. MUST NOT retry the action without submitting a new CAR.
          </dd>
        </dl>

        <h3>5.2 Decision Envelope Fields</h3>

        <dl>
          <dt>decision <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. One of: <code>ALLOW</code>, <code>DENY</code>, <code>DEFER</code>,
            <code>REVOKE</code>.
          </dd>

          <dt>action_id <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String (UUID v4). MUST match the <code>action_id</code> from the submitted CAR.
            Enforcement points MUST verify this match before acting on the decision.
          </dd>

          <dt>evaluated_at <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String (ISO 8601, UTC). The timestamp at which the decision was made.
          </dd>

          <dt>policy_version <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. An opaque version string identifying the policy under which this decision was made.
            Used in Cryptographic Attestation of Consent. MUST be recorded in audit logs.
          </dd>

          <dt>expires_at <span class="field-tag conditional">CONDITIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String (ISO 8601). REQUIRED when <code>decision</code> is <code>ALLOW</code>. The
            enforcement point MUST NOT execute the action after this timestamp.
          </dd>

          <dt>reason_code <span class="field-tag conditional">CONDITIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. REQUIRED when <code>decision</code> is <code>DENY</code> or
            <code>REVOKE</code>. A machine-readable code identifying why the action was denied.
          </dd>

          <dt>reason_detail <span class="field-tag optional">OPTIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. Human-readable explanation of the denial or revocation reason.
          </dd>

          <dt>defer_payload <span class="field-tag conditional">CONDITIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            Object. REQUIRED when <code>decision</code> is <code>DEFER</code>. See Section 5.3.
          </dd>
        </dl>

        <h3>5.3 The defer_payload Object</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>defer_payload.resume_token <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. An opaque token the enforcement point uses to poll for or receive the
            ApprovalDecision. MUST be treated as a secret in transit.
          </dd>

          <dt>defer_payload.approver_endpoint <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String (URI). The HTTPS URL of the approver interface that will render and process this
            action. MUST use HTTPS.
          </dd>

          <dt>defer_payload.expires_at <span class="field-tag required">REQUIRED</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String (ISO 8601). If approval is not received by this time, the enforcement point MUST
            treat the action as DENY.
          </dd>

          <dt>defer_payload.approver_hint <span class="field-tag optional">OPTIONAL</span></dt>
          <dd>
            String. Human-readable description of who should approve this action. Not authoritative;
            for display purposes only.
          </dd>
        </dl>

        <h3>5.4 Full Decision Envelope JSON Schema</h3>

        <pre><code>&#123;
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://machineauthority.org/schema/decision-envelope/v0.1",
  "title": "Decision Envelope",
  "description": "The response from the Action Authorization Boundary to a submitted CAR.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["decision", "action_id", "evaluated_at", "policy_version"],
  "properties": &#123;
    "decision": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["ALLOW", "DENY", "DEFER", "REVOKE"],
      "description": "REQUIRED. The authorization decision."
    &#125;,
    "action_id": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "format": "uuid",
      "description": "REQUIRED. MUST match the action_id from the submitted CAR."
    &#125;,
    "evaluated_at": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "REQUIRED. ISO 8601 timestamp at which the decision was made."
    &#125;,
    "policy_version": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "description": "REQUIRED. An opaque version string identifying the policy under which this decision was made. Used in Cryptographic Attestation of Consent."
    &#125;,
    "expires_at": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "CONDITIONAL. REQUIRED when decision is ALLOW. The enforcement point MUST NOT execute the action after this timestamp."
    &#125;,
    "reason_code": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "description": "CONDITIONAL. REQUIRED when decision is DENY or REVOKE. A machine-readable code identifying why the action was denied."
    &#125;,
    "reason_detail": &#123;
      "type": "string",
      "description": "OPTIONAL. Human-readable explanation of the denial reason."
    &#125;,
    "defer_payload": &#123;
      "type": "object",
      "description": "CONDITIONAL. REQUIRED when decision is DEFER. Contains the information needed to route the action to an approver.",
      "required": ["resume_token", "approver_endpoint", "expires_at"],
      "properties": &#123;
        "resume_token": &#123;
          "type": "string",
          "description": "An opaque token the enforcement point uses to poll for or receive the ApprovalDecision."
        &#125;,
        "approver_endpoint": &#123;
          "type": "string",
          "format": "uri",
          "description": "The HTTPS URL of the approver interface that will render and process this action."
        &#125;,
        "expires_at": &#123;
          "type": "string",
          "format": "date-time",
          "description": "If approval is not received by this time, the enforcement point MUST treat the action as DENY."
        &#125;,
        "approver_hint": &#123;
          "type": "string",
          "description": "OPTIONAL. Human-readable description of who should approve this action."
        &#125;
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="examples">
        <h2>6. Example Payloads</h2>

        <h3>6.1 ALLOW — Filesystem Read</h3>
        <p>
          A data pipeline agent reads a configuration file. The operation is read-only and within the
          agent's granted scope; the AAB returns ALLOW with a 30-second expiry.
        </p>

        <p class="example-label">CAR Payload</p>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "car_version": "0.1",
  "action_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
  "tool_name": "filesystem/read_file",
  "arguments": &#123;
    "path": "/var/app/config.json",
    "encoding": "utf-8"
  &#125;,
  "actor": &#123;
    "identity": &#123; "type": "spiffe", "uri": "spiffe://acme.com/agents/data-pipeline/prod" &#125;,
    "delegation_chain": [
      &#123; "type": "did", "did": "did:web:acme.com:users:alice" &#125;
    ]
  &#125;,
  "session_id": "sess_7f3k2m9p",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-02T14:23:07Z"
&#125;</code></pre>

        <p class="example-label">Decision Envelope</p>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "decision": "ALLOW",
  "action_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
  "evaluated_at": "2026-05-02T14:23:07.042Z",
  "policy_version": "prod-policy-v2.4.1",
  "expires_at": "2026-05-02T14:23:37Z"
&#125;</code></pre>

        <h3>6.2 DEFER — Financial Transfer Requiring Human Approval</h3>
        <p>
          A finance agent attempts a wire transfer of $475.00 on behalf of a human principal through
          an orchestrator. The operation exceeds the autonomous approval threshold; the AAB returns
          DEFER and routes to the finance team lead for review.
        </p>

        <p class="example-label">CAR Payload</p>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "car_version": "0.1",
  "action_id": "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901",
  "tool_name": "stripe/create_transfer",
  "arguments": &#123;
    "amount": 47500,
    "currency": "usd",
    "destination": "acct_1Rab2kLkdIwHu7ix",
    "description": "Invoice #2847 settlement"
  &#125;,
  "actor": &#123;
    "identity": &#123; "type": "spiffe", "uri": "spiffe://acme.com/agents/finance-agent/prod" &#125;,
    "delegation_chain": [
      &#123; "type": "did", "did": "did:web:acme.com:users:bob" &#125;,
      &#123; "type": "spiffe", "uri": "spiffe://acme.com/agents/orchestrator/prod" &#125;
    ],
    "agent_version": "2.1.4"
  &#125;,
  "session_id": "sess_9g4m3n1q",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-02T14:25:11Z",
  "policy_context": &#123;
    "risk_tier": "high",
    "environment": "production"
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>

        <p class="example-label">Decision Envelope</p>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "decision": "DEFER",
  "action_id": "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901",
  "evaluated_at": "2026-05-02T14:25:11.018Z",
  "policy_version": "prod-policy-v2.4.1",
  "defer_payload": &#123;
    "resume_token": "rt_7kXmQ9pN2vR4sT8wY1jL",
    "approver_endpoint": "https://approvals.acme.com/review",
    "expires_at": "2026-05-02T14:55:11Z",
    "approver_hint": "Finance team lead (transfers > $400)"
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>

        <h3>6.3 DENY — Destructive DDL Operation Outside Policy Bounds</h3>
        <p>
          A cleanup agent operating in staging identity attempts to DROP a table in the production
          database. The AAB denies: the agent's identity scope does not include destructive DDL
          operations on production, and no DEFER path is available for this reason code.
        </p>

        <p class="example-label">CAR Payload</p>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "car_version": "0.1",
  "action_id": "c3d4e5f6-a7b8-9012-cdef-123456789012",
  "tool_name": "database/execute_query",
  "arguments": &#123;
    "query": "DROP TABLE user_sessions",
    "database": "production_db"
  &#125;,
  "actor": &#123;
    "identity": &#123; "type": "spiffe", "uri": "spiffe://acme.com/agents/cleanup-agent/staging" &#125;
  &#125;,
  "session_id": "sess_2h5n4o2r",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-02T14:27:33Z"
&#125;</code></pre>

        <p class="example-label">Decision Envelope</p>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "decision": "DENY",
  "action_id": "c3d4e5f6-a7b8-9012-cdef-123456789012",
  "evaluated_at": "2026-05-02T14:27:33.003Z",
  "policy_version": "prod-policy-v2.4.1",
  "reason_code": "DESTRUCTIVE_OP_NOT_AUTHORIZED",
  "reason_detail": "DDL DROP operations on production databases require DEFER with DBA approval. This agent identity does not have destructive operation scope."
&#125;</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="security">
        <h2>7. Security Considerations</h2>

        <h3>7.1 Action ID Uniqueness</h3>
        <p>
          CAR payloads MUST NOT be cached or reused. Each proposed action MUST produce a new
          <code>action_id</code>. Policy engines may reject CARs with previously seen action IDs as
          a replay defense.
        </p>

        <h3>7.2 Decision Envelope Binding</h3>
        <p>
          Enforcement points MUST verify that the <code>action_id</code> in the Decision Envelope
          matches the submitted CAR before acting on the decision. A mismatch indicates a routing
          error or active tampering; the enforcement point MUST abort and alert.
        </p>

        <h3>7.3 Argument Integrity</h3>
        <p>
          The <code>arguments</code> field MUST contain the exact arguments that will be passed to
          the tool at execution. Any modification of arguments between evaluation and execution
          invalidates the authorization. Enforcement points MUST pass the arguments field from the
          CAR directly to the tool call without transformation.
        </p>

        <h3>7.4 ALLOW Expiry</h3>
        <p>
          When <code>decision</code> is <code>ALLOW</code>, the enforcement point MUST check
          <code>expires_at</code> before execution. An expired ALLOW MUST be treated as DENY. The
          enforcement point MUST NOT re-submit the original CAR to obtain a fresh decision; it MUST
          generate a new CAR with a new <code>action_id</code>.
        </p>

        <h3>7.5 Actor Identity Verification</h3>
        <p>
          The <code>actor.identity</code> field SHOULD be verified against the cryptographic
          credential presented by the agent (e.g., a SPIFFE SVID X.509 certificate, a signed DID
          document). Unverified identity strings are advisory only and MUST NOT be treated as
          authoritative by policy engines that require strong identity guarantees.
        </p>

        <h3>7.6 DEFER Expiry</h3>
        <p>
          DEFER decisions with expired resume tokens (past <code>defer_payload.expires_at</code>)
          MUST be treated as DENY. The enforcement point MUST NOT proceed to execution on the basis
          of an approval received after this deadline, even if the approver interface accepted the
          approval.
        </p>

        <h3>7.7 Resume Token Confidentiality</h3>
        <p>
          The <code>resume_token</code> issued in a DEFER decision grants the ability to poll for or
          receive an ApprovalDecision. It MUST be treated as a bearer secret: transmitted only over
          TLS, stored with the same controls as session credentials, and invalidated by the AAB after
          the decision is delivered or the expiry is reached.
        </p>
      </section>

